---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

const markup = `<table class="bo-data-table" data-row-edit>
  <thead><tr>
    <th scope="col">Item</th>
    <th scope="col" class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">Qty</th>
    <th scope="col" class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">Unit price</th>
    <th scope="col"><span class="bo-visually-hidden">Actions</span></th>
  </tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr data-row-id="LINE-1">
      <td>
        <!-- Combobox in a cell: no special wiring, just the normal markup -->
        <div class="bo-combobox">
          <input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless" role="combobox" id="line-1-item"
              aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="line-1-list" aria-autocomplete="list"
              autocomplete="off" aria-label="Item" value="Steel bracket, 40mm" />
          <ul class="bo-combobox__listbox" id="line-1-list" role="listbox" popover>
            <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" data-value="SKU-4021">Steel bracket, 40mm</li>
            <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" data-value="SKU-4022">Steel bracket, 60mm</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </td>
      <td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">
        <!-- Cell-level error: .bo-form-field wraps the input + message pair
             (the SAME contract as a standalone form field — no new CSS) -->
        <div class="bo-form-field" style="margin-block-end: 0">
          <input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless bo-input--numeric" type="number"
              value="450" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="line-1-qty-err"
              aria-label="Quantity" />
          <span class="bo-form-field__message" id="line-1-qty-err" role="alert">Exceeds on-hand (200)</span>
        </div>
      </td>
      <td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">
        <input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless bo-input--numeric" type="number"
            step="0.01" value="3.40" aria-label="Unit price" />
      </td>
      <td class="bo-data-table__row-edit-actions">
        <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning" data-row-edit-dirty hidden>Unsaved</span>
        <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm" type="button" data-row-edit-save hidden>Save</button>
        <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" type="button" data-row-edit-cancel hidden>Cancel</button>
        <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--danger-ghost" type="button" data-line-remove aria-label="Remove line">✕</button>
      </td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
<button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary" type="button" data-line-add>+ Add line</button>

<script type="module">
  import { initRowEdit, initCombobox } from "@busy-office/ui/js";
  initRowEdit(); initCombobox();     // once — delegation covers rows added later

  // Add/remove a line is plain app logic, not a framework behavior — the
  // framework has no opinion on WHERE new rows come from (a <template>
  // clone here; your app might fetch a fragment from the server instead).
  let n = 1;
  document.querySelector("[data-line-add]").addEventListener("click", () => {
    n += 1;
    const tbody = document.querySelector("[data-row-edit] tbody");
    const row = document.getElementById("line-template").content.cloneNode(true);
    const tr = row.querySelector("tr");
    tr.dataset.rowId = \`LINE-\${n}\`;
    // Combobox listbox ids must be unique per row — reusing one id across
    // cloned rows is the exact collision bug fixed 2026-08-15 (widget #2
    // silently driving widget #1). Give each clone its own pair.
    const list = row.querySelector("ul");
    list.id = \`line-\${n}-list\`;
    row.querySelector('[role="combobox"]').setAttribute("aria-controls", list.id);
    tbody.appendChild(row);
    tbody.lastElementChild.querySelector("input").focus();
    // No re-init call: initRowEdit()/initCombobox() are document-level
    // delegation — the new row's input and combobox work immediately.
  });
  document.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
    const btn = e.target.closest("[data-line-remove]");
    if (btn) btn.closest("tr").remove();
  });
</script>`;
---
<Gallery title="Pattern: editable grid">
  <p class="demo-note">
    Line-item entry — a PO, an invoice, a pick list — composed entirely from
    existing pieces, presented as a graded path. <strong>Simple</strong>:
    plain text/number cells with dirty-state + Save/Cancel — that's the
    <a href={base + '/components/data-table'}>data-table page's multi-row
    inline edit</a>, start there. <strong>Medium</strong> (first demo below):
    a combobox lookup cell, cell-level validation, add/remove lines.
    <strong>Money &amp; unit cells</strong>: currency and unit as real
    separate fields inside a row. <strong>Advanced</strong>: every cell
    type, realtime totals, and the save-per-change mode. <strong>The full
    picture</strong>: a composite PO line-items editor putting all of it
    in one table. Zero new CSS at every
    step — the grid is the same primitives, composed harder.
  </p>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Medium — combobox lookup cells, validation, add/remove lines</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-row-edit id="eg-table">
        <thead><tr>
          <th scope="col">Item</th>
          <th scope="col" class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">Qty</th>
          <th scope="col" class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">Unit price</th>
          <th scope="col"><span class="bo-visually-hidden">Actions</span></th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr data-row-id="LINE-1">
            <td>
              <div class="bo-combobox">
                <input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless" role="combobox" id="line-1-item"
                    aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="line-1-list" aria-autocomplete="list"
                    autocomplete="off" aria-label="Item" value="Steel bracket, 40mm" />
                <ul class="bo-combobox__listbox" id="line-1-list" role="listbox" popover>
                  <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" data-value="SKU-4021">Steel bracket, 40mm</li>
                  <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" data-value="SKU-4022">Steel bracket, 60mm</li>
                </ul>
              </div>
            </td>
            <td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">
              <div class="bo-form-field" style="margin-block-end: 0">
                <input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless bo-input--numeric" type="number"
                    value="450" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="line-1-qty-err"
                    aria-label="Quantity" />
                <span class="bo-form-field__message" id="line-1-qty-err" role="alert">Exceeds on-hand (200)</span>
              </div>
            </td>
            <td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">
              <input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless bo-input--numeric" type="number"
                  step="0.01" value="3.40" aria-label="Unit price" />
            </td>
            <td class="bo-data-table__row-edit-actions">
              <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning" data-row-edit-dirty hidden>Unsaved</span>
              <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm" type="button" data-row-edit-save hidden>Save</button>
              <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" type="button" data-row-edit-cancel hidden>Cancel</button>
              <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--danger-ghost" type="button" data-line-remove aria-label="Remove line">✕</button>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <template id="eg-template">
      <tr data-row-id="">
        <td>
          <div class="bo-combobox">
            <input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless" role="combobox"
                aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="line-1-list" aria-autocomplete="list"
                autocomplete="off" aria-label="Item" placeholder="Search items…" />
            <ul class="bo-combobox__listbox" id="line-1-list" role="listbox" popover>
              <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" data-value="SKU-4021">Steel bracket, 40mm</li>
              <li class="bo-combobox__option" role="option" data-value="SKU-4022">Steel bracket, 60mm</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </td>
        <td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">
          <input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless bo-input--numeric" type="number" value="0" aria-label="Quantity" />
        </td>
        <td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">
          <input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless bo-input--numeric" type="number" step="0.01" value="0.00" aria-label="Unit price" />
        </td>
        <td class="bo-data-table__row-edit-actions">
          <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning" data-row-edit-dirty hidden>Unsaved</span>
          <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm" type="button" data-row-edit-save hidden>Save</button>
          <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" type="button" data-row-edit-cancel hidden>Cancel</button>
          <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--danger-ghost" type="button" data-line-remove aria-label="Remove line">✕</button>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </template>
    <p style="margin-block-start: var(--bo-space-3)">
      <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary" type="button" id="eg-add">+ Add line</button>
    </p>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Try it: the Qty cell above starts invalid (exceeds
    on-hand) — the message is a normal <code>.bo-form-field__message</code>, just
    at cell granularity. Pick an option in the Item combobox: it marks the row
    dirty exactly like typing does (2026-08-15 fix — committing an option now
    fires a real <code>input</code> event, not just <code>bo:combobox-select</code>,
    so it composes with any generic field listener). Add a line: the new row's
    combobox and inline edit work immediately, no re-init call.</p>
  </section>

  <script>
    import { initRowEdit, initCombobox, initMoneyField, initQuantity, initTableSum, initTagInput, currencyDecimals } from '@busy-office/ui/js';
    // One consolidated init block — this page demos five behaviors, all
    // document-level delegations, called once each in any order.
    initRowEdit();
    initCombobox();
    initMoneyField();
    initQuantity();
    initTableSum();
    initTagInput();
    let n = 1;
    document.getElementById('eg-add').addEventListener('click', () => {
      n += 1;
      const tpl = document.getElementById('eg-template') as HTMLTemplateElement;
      const frag = tpl.content.cloneNode(true) as DocumentFragment;
      const row = frag.querySelector('tr')!;
      row.dataset.rowId = `LINE-${n}`;
      const list = row.querySelector('ul')!;
      const combo = row.querySelector('input[role="combobox"]')!;
      list.id = `line-${n}-list`;
      combo.setAttribute('aria-controls', list.id);
      document.querySelector('#eg-table tbody')!.appendChild(row);
      (row.querySelector('input') as HTMLElement).focus();
    });
    document.getElementById('eg-table')!.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
      const btn = (e.target as Element).closest('[data-line-remove]');
      if (btn) btn.closest('tr')!.remove();
    });

    // Tag chips are consumer data: append on add (rejecting duplicates),
    // snapshot per row, restore on bo:row-cancel.
    const snapshots = new Map<string, string>();
    for (const el of document.querySelectorAll('.bo-tag-input')) {
      const id = el.id;
      if (id) snapshots.set(id, el.innerHTML);
    }
    document.addEventListener('bo:tag-add', (e) => {
      const group = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('.bo-tag-input');
      if (!group || !group.closest('#eg-adv-table')) return;
      const value = (e as CustomEvent).detail.value;
      const exists = [...group.querySelectorAll('.bo-tag-input__tag')]
        .some((t) => t.textContent!.replace('×', '').trim() === value);
      if (exists) return;
      const tag = document.createElement('span');
      tag.className = 'bo-tag-input__tag';
      tag.textContent = value;
      const rm = document.createElement('button');
      rm.className = 'bo-tag-input__remove';
      rm.type = 'button';
      rm.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Remove ' + value);
      rm.textContent = '×';
      tag.append(rm);
      group.insertBefore(tag, group.querySelector('.bo-tag-input__field'));
    });
    document.addEventListener('bo:row-cancel', (e) => {
      const row = (e as CustomEvent).detail.row as HTMLElement;
      for (const group of row.querySelectorAll('.bo-tag-input')) {
        const snap = snapshots.get(group.id);
        if (snap !== undefined) group.innerHTML = snap;
      }
    });
    document.addEventListener('bo:row-save', (e) => {
      const { row, rowId } = (e as CustomEvent).detail;
      // re-snapshot saved tag state so a later Cancel returns HERE
      for (const group of row.querySelectorAll('.bo-tag-input')) {
        if (group.id) snapshots.set(group.id, group.innerHTML);
      }
      if (row.closest('#eg-live-table')) {
        const log = document.getElementById('eg-live-log')!;
        log.textContent = `Saved ${rowId} at ${new Date().toLocaleTimeString()} — wire this to fetch/hx-patch in a real app.`;
      }
    });

    // Composite editor: line totals + grand total are CUSTOM math on the
    // bo:cell-change feed (qty × price, formatted per that row's currency
    // via the exported currencyDecimals) — the half of the subtotal
    // contract data-sum-of can't express. Restores announce themselves,
    // so Cancel walks the computed cells back through this same listener.
    const compTable = document.getElementById('eg-comp-table');
    function recomputeComposite() {
      if (!compTable) return;
      const currencies = new Set<string>();
      let grand = 0;
      let grandDecimals = 0;
      for (const row of compTable.querySelectorAll('tbody tr')) {
        const qty = Number((row.querySelector('[name="qty"]') as HTMLInputElement)?.value) || 0;
        const price = Number((row.querySelector('[name="price"]') as HTMLInputElement)?.value) || 0;
        const cur = (row.querySelector('[name="cur"]') as HTMLSelectElement)?.value ?? 'USD';
        const d = currencyDecimals(cur);
        const total = qty * price;
        const cell = row.querySelector('[data-line-total]');
        if (cell) cell.textContent = total.toFixed(d);
        currencies.add(cur);
        grand += total;
        grandDecimals = Math.max(grandDecimals, d);
      }
      const grandCell = document.getElementById('comp-grand');
      if (grandCell)
        grandCell.textContent =
          currencies.size === 1 ? grand.toFixed(grandDecimals) : 'mixed';
    }
    document.addEventListener('bo:cell-change', (e) => {
      if ((e.target as Element).closest('#eg-comp-table')) recomputeComposite();
    });

    // Committed-change announcements (grill E4): visible totals update per
    // keystroke for sighted users; the hidden status speaks ONE summary per
    // committed edit (change = blur for text, immediate for select/
    // checkbox/stepper) — never a queue of per-keystroke announcements.
    document.addEventListener('change', (e) => {
      const target = e.target as Element;
      const adv = target.closest('#eg-adv-table');
      if (adv) {
        const status = document.getElementById('eg-adv-status')!;
        status.textContent = `Total quantity ${adv.querySelector('[data-sum-of="qty"]')!.textContent}`;
      }
      const comp = target.closest('#eg-comp-table');
      if (comp) {
        const row = target.closest('tr');
        const line = row?.querySelector('[data-line-total]')?.textContent;
        const status = document.getElementById('eg-comp-status')!;
        status.textContent =
          (line ? `Line total ${line}; ` : '') +
          `total quantity ${comp.querySelector('[data-sum-of="qty"]')!.textContent}; ` +
          `grand total ${document.getElementById('comp-grand')!.textContent}`;
      }
    });
  </script>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Money &amp; unit cells — currency/unit as real separate fields</h2>
    <p>An editable line often needs the currency or unit editable <em>next
    to</em> the number, not baked into a label. Both compose into a
    <code>data-row-edit</code> row with zero special wiring — and their
    precision behaviors keep working: switch this row's currency to JPY and
    the price reformats to 0 decimals, marks the row dirty, and
    <strong>Cancel restores the currency, the value, and the
    precision</strong> together.</p>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-row-edit id="eg-money-table">
        <thead><tr>
          <th scope="col">Item</th>
          <th scope="col" class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">Qty</th>
          <th scope="col" class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">Unit price</th>
          <th scope="col"><span class="bo-visually-hidden">Actions</span></th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr data-row-id="LINE-M1">
            <td>Hydraulic pump, 20&nbsp;bar</td>
            <td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">
              <div class="bo-quantity" style="max-inline-size: 14rem">
                <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary bo-quantity__step" type="button" data-quantity-step="-1" aria-label="Decrease quantity">&minus;</button>
                <input class="bo-quantity__input bo-input--seamless" type="number" value="2.50" min="0" step="0.01" inputmode="decimal" aria-label="Quantity" />
                <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary bo-quantity__step" type="button" data-quantity-step="1" aria-label="Increase quantity">+</button>
                <select class="bo-select bo-quantity__unit-select" aria-label="Unit">
                  <option selected>kg</option><option>each</option><option>box</option>
                </select>
              </div>
            </td>
            <td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">
              <div class="bo-money">
                <select class="bo-select bo-money__currency" aria-label="Currency">
                  <option selected>USD</option><option>SGD</option><option>JPY</option><option>KWD</option>
                </select>
                <input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless bo-money__amount" type="number" step="0.01" value="1250.00" aria-label="Unit price" />
              </div>
            </td>
            <td class="bo-data-table__row-edit-actions">
              <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning" data-row-edit-dirty hidden>Unsaved</span>
              <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm" type="button" data-row-edit-save hidden>Save</button>
              <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" type="button" data-row-edit-cancel hidden>Cancel</button>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Under the hood: the money/unit behaviors
    dispatch a real <code>input</code> event when they reformat, so
    <code>initRowEdit()</code>'s dirty tracking sees precision changes the
    same as typing; Cancel re-fires <code>change</code> on a reset select so
    the precision re-derives from the restored currency/unit instead of
    sticking at the abandoned one.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Advanced — every cell type + realtime totals</h2>
    <p>All the common ERP column types in one editable table: text, a
    native <code>&lt;select&gt;</code>, date, checkbox, and a tag-input
    cell — plus a footer total that recomputes in realtime
    (<code>initTableSum()</code>, declarative <code>data-sum-of</code>).
    Edit the Qty fields and watch the total; toggle, retag, then Cancel —
    native fields restore themselves, and the <code>bo:row-cancel</code>
    hook restores the chips.</p>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-row-edit id="eg-adv-table">
        <thead><tr>
          <th scope="col">Line</th>
          <th scope="col" class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">Qty</th>
          <th scope="col">Status</th>
          <th scope="col">Needed by</th>
          <th scope="col">Rush</th>
          <th scope="col">Cost centers</th>
          <th scope="col"><span class="bo-visually-hidden">Actions</span></th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr data-row-id="ADV-1">
            <td><input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless" name="line" value="Bearing kit" aria-label="Line description" /></td>
            <td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">
              <input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless bo-input--numeric" name="qty" type="number" step="0.01" value="2.50" aria-label="Quantity" />
            </td>
            <td>
              <select class="bo-select" name="status" aria-label="Status">
                <option selected>Open</option><option>Approved</option><option>On hold</option>
              </select>
            </td>
            <td><input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless" name="due" type="date" value="2026-08-30" aria-label="Needed by" /></td>
            <td><input class="bo-checkbox" name="rush" type="checkbox" aria-label="Rush order" /></td>
            <td>
              <div class="bo-tag-input" id="adv-1-tags" role="group" aria-label="Cost centers — Bearing kit">
                <span class="bo-tag-input__tag">CC-4021<button class="bo-tag-input__remove" type="button" aria-label="Remove CC-4021">×</button></span>
                <input class="bo-tag-input__field" type="text" placeholder="Add…" aria-label="Add cost center — Bearing kit" />
              </div>
            </td>
            <td class="bo-data-table__row-edit-actions">
              <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning" data-row-edit-dirty hidden>Unsaved</span>
              <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm" type="button" data-row-edit-save aria-label="Save — Bearing kit" hidden>Save</button>
              <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" type="button" data-row-edit-cancel aria-label="Cancel — Bearing kit" hidden>Cancel</button>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr data-row-id="ADV-2">
            <td><input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless" name="line" value="Seal ring set" aria-label="Line description" /></td>
            <td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric">
              <input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless bo-input--numeric" name="qty" type="number" step="0.01" value="5.00" aria-label="Quantity" />
            </td>
            <td>
              <select class="bo-select" name="status" aria-label="Status">
                <option>Open</option><option selected>Approved</option><option>On hold</option>
              </select>
            </td>
            <td><input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless" name="due" type="date" value="2026-09-05" aria-label="Needed by" /></td>
            <td><input class="bo-checkbox" name="rush" type="checkbox" checked aria-label="Rush order" /></td>
            <td>
              <div class="bo-tag-input" id="adv-2-tags" role="group" aria-label="Cost centers — Seal ring set">
                <span class="bo-tag-input__tag">CC-1180<button class="bo-tag-input__remove" type="button" aria-label="Remove CC-1180">×</button></span>
                <input class="bo-tag-input__field" type="text" placeholder="Add…" aria-label="Add cost center — Seal ring set" />
              </div>
            </td>
            <td class="bo-data-table__row-edit-actions">
              <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning" data-row-edit-dirty hidden>Unsaved</span>
              <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm" type="button" data-row-edit-save aria-label="Save — Seal ring set" hidden>Save</button>
              <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--sm bo-btn--secondary" type="button" data-row-edit-cancel aria-label="Cancel — Seal ring set" hidden>Cancel</button>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
        <tfoot><tr>
          <td class="bo-data-table__col--right">Total qty</td>
          <td class="bo-data-table__col--numeric" data-sum-of="qty">7.50</td>
          <td colspan="5"></td>
        </tr></tfoot>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-visually-hidden" id="eg-adv-status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Subtotals come in <strong>both modes</strong>:
    declarative auto-sum (<code>data-sum-of="qty"</code>, shown above — a
    deliberate, documented exception to "you do the data") or listen to
    <code>bo:cell-change</code> (<code>rowId</code>/<code>field</code>/<code>value</code>
    on every committed edit) and do custom math — qty × price line totals,
    weighted sums, whatever the auto mode can't express. Tag chips are
    consumer-rendered, so Cancel can't restore them natively —
    <code>bo:row-cancel</code> fires after the native fields reset,
    exactly for that. <strong>Announce totals on COMMITTED change, not per
    keystroke</strong>: the visible cells update in realtime for sighted
    users, while a visually-hidden <code>aria-live="polite"</code> status
    (see this page's script) speaks one summary per committed edit —
    <code>change</code> fires on blur for text, immediately for
    select/checkbox/stepper — instead of a queue of announcements on every
    keystroke. The summary includes the edited line's total, giving line
    totals the same announcement parity as the grand total.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>WYSIWYG — display-identical until you touch it</h2>
    <p>Every control seamless: at rest the table is pixel-comparable to a
    plain read-only data table — no borders, no chevrons, no field
    chrome. Hover a cell and its affordance appears; focus it and the
    field wakes fully. <code>.bo-input--seamless</code> has done this for
    text/number/date since the first editable grid; this adds the same
    <em>setting</em> to the remaining cell types —
    <code>.bo-select--seamless</code> and
    <code>.bo-tag-input--seamless</code> (a checkbox already reads
    identically in both modes; a combobox cell is
    <code>.bo-input--seamless</code> on its input). Deliberately
    <strong>not</strong> a display↔editor swap engine: the control never
    changes, so the keyboard path and screen-reader semantics never
    change either — that's the whole trick. <strong>Scope</strong>: the
    compound cells stay chromed on purpose — Money/Quantity's
    currency/unit selects share an edge with their input, and stepper
    buttons are actions, not values; a compound control without its
    boundaries stops reading as one control. WYSIWYG covers the
    single-control cell types shown below.</p>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-row-edit id="eg-wys-table">
